 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the Honorable Joseph J. Maltese to receive compensation\nand service credit",
    "basePrintNo": "S9295",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9295-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9295\n\nSPONSOR: SCARCELLA-SPANTON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize the Honorable Joseph J. Maltese to receive compen-\nsation and service credit\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. States the determination of the legislature and office of\ncourt administration to compensate Joseph J. Maltese, Justice for the\nAppellate Division of the Second Department of the Supreme Court, for\nhis unnecessary dismissal serving the people of the State of New York.\n\nSection 2. Authorizes the Office of Court Administration to pay Justice\nJoseph J. Maltese the salary he would have earned from January 1st,\n2021, to November 7th, 2021. Section two also lays out provision other\nearnings and the Justice's pension.\n\nSection 3. This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnder New York State Law, Justices over the age of seventy must request\ncertification to continue to serve. In 2020, a number of justices were\ndenied this certification based on budget cuts that never came to frui-\ntion. Since then, justices have been fairly compensated by the Office of\nCourt Administration, with Justice Maltese having been left out. There\nis no denying that Justice Maltese has faithfully served his community\nand that failure to have compensated him for his time is an affront to\nthat dutiful service to the state.\n\nThe bill would authorize Justice Maltese to be paid the salary he would\nhave earned from January 1st, 2021, to November 7th, 2021, just as\nfellow Justices in his same condition have been since they were reau-\nthorized by the Governor. It is essential that Justice Maltese be reme-\ndied any damages done onto him due to this oversight and that his situ-\nation be made whole with due compensation in terms of salary and\npension.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee attached fiscal note in bill language.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis legislation will take effect immediately.\n",
